  "label": "Military spouse stereotype",
  "description": "The meme relies on a stereotype that military spouses, particularly those over 30, are often overlooked, unappreciated, or stuck in repetitive, unfulfilling situations. This stereotype is not universally true but is commonly used in popular culture and social discourse to frame the experience of military spouses, often ignoring the sacrifices, resilience, and diverse realities of this group.",
